%% Event flow — import completes, derived analytics refresh, failure and replay.
%% Guarantees: event is written in the SAME PostgreSQL transaction as the ledger change (outbox);
%% delivery is at-least-once; consumers are idempotent (inbox) -> effectively-once results.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant API as Ingestion / Ledger (Spring Boot)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant REG as Event publication registry (Spring Modulith)
    participant C1 as Consumer: analytics-refresh
    participant C2 as Consumer: audit-writer
    participant REC as Go reconciler (nightly)

    B->>API: POST /api/upload/csv (Idempotency-Key)
    API->>DB: UploadJob = PENDING
    API-->>B: 202 + job id
    Note over API: async worker parses, de-duplicates by fingerprint
    rect rgb(235, 245, 235)
    Note over API,DB: ONE local ACID transaction
    API->>DB: INSERT new transactions (unique fingerprint index)
    API->>DB: UPDATE upload_job = COMPLETED
    API->>REG: publish ImportCompleted v1 + LedgerPeriodChanged v1
    REG->>DB: INSERT event_publication rows (same tx)
    end
    DB-->>REG: commit
    par each listener gets its own publication row
        REG->>C1: deliver ImportCompleted
        C1->>DB: BEGIN, INSERT processed_event (consumer, event_id), on conflict skip
        C1->>DB: recompute analytics for affected months, COMMIT
        C1-->>REG: mark publication complete
    and
        REG->>C2: deliver ImportCompleted
        C2->>DB: append audit record (idempotent by event_id)
        C2-->>REG: mark complete
    end

    alt listener throws / process crashes
        REG->>REG: publication stays incomplete
        Note over REG: re-submitted on restart and by a scheduled retry with backoff
        REG->>C1: redeliver (same event_id)
        C1->>DB: inbox hit -> no duplicate effect
    end
    alt still failing after N attempts
        REG->>DB: mark FAILED / copy to dead-letter table + alert
        Note over API: operator fixes cause, replays by id or time range
    end

    REC->>DB: read-only: re-aggregate ledger independently
    REC->>DB: compare with analytics schema
    REC-->>API: report (JSON): zero delta required, else alert

    Note over REG,C1: Later, only if the broker gate fires (docs 05 section 7):<br/>a relay publishes outbox rows to Kafka; consumers keep the same inbox
